@startuml
title Halo — incrementally verifiable computation, end to end
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  DiamondBorderColor #7A5BB5
  ArrowColor #7A5BB5
  StartColor #7A5BB5
  EndColor #7A5BB5
}

|Prover|
start
repeat
  :apply the transition function F to the current state;
  :commit to the witness polynomials\nwith Pedersen vector commitments;
  :run the inner product argument\nto open every commitment at the challenge points;
  :derive all challenges with Fiat-Shamir,\nhashing the transcript with Rescue;
  :inside the verification circuit:\ntake the previous deferred state as public input;
  :partially verify the previous proof, in O(log d);
  :amortise: merge the new G into the deferred state;
  :emit the updated deferred state as public output;
  :switch to the partner curve for the next step;
repeat while (more steps to prove?) is (yes) not (no)
:publish the final proof, 3.5 KiB,\ncarrying the final deferred state;

|Ultimate verifier|
:check the final proof, in O(log d);
:perform the deferred linear MSM exactly once, in O(d);
if (does the deferred check pass?) then (yes)
  :accept the entire T-step computation;
else (no)
  :reject;
endif
stop
@enduml
